================================================================
FINDINGS
================================================================

CONFIRMED VULNERABLE (1 instance):
-----------------------------------
File: InCallController.java:2261 (service-telecom.jar)
Method: serviceClassExists(ServiceInfo, UserHandle)
Code: createPackageContextAsUser(serviceInfo.packageName, 3, userHandle)
Flag: 3 = CONTEXT_INCLUDE_CODE | CONTEXT_IGNORE_SECURITY
Trigger: TelecomManager.addCall() → InCallController.onCallAdded()
Reachable by unprivileged app: YES (MANAGE_OWN_CALLS auto-granted)
Status: EXPLOITED — system_server code execution proven

ALL OTHER createPackageContext/createPackageContextAsUser calls:
---------------------------------------------------------------
Every other call found across all analyzed JARs uses flag 0 (no special context),
or flag 4 (CONTEXT_RESTRICTED). None use CONTEXT_INCLUDE_CODE.

Specific counts:
- service-telecom.jar: 8 calls, only InCallController uses flag 3
- service-permission.jar: 7 calls, all flag 0
- framework-nfc.jar: 0 calls
- services.jar: 30+ calls, all flag 0 (or 4 in one case: ActivityRecord)
- service-wifi.jar: 3 calls, all flag 0
- framework-telecom.jar: 0 calls
- framework-telephony.jar: 0 calls
- service-media-s.jar: 0 calls
- framework.jar: 3 calls in DEX, all flag 0 or 4

AppComponentFactory references in services.jar:
- BinaryTransparencyService.java:405 — logging only, not execution

Class loading from untrusted packages:
- All ClassLoader/Class.forName usage in services.jar loads from system's
  own class loader, not from untrusted app packages

================================================================
CONCLUSION
================================================================

The InCallController.serviceClassExists() is the ONLY instance across
all analyzed system JARs on the Pixel Watch 2 that uses
createPackageContextAsUser with CONTEXT_INCLUDE_CODE on an untrusted
package name. No additional similar vulnerabilities found in the
scanned system services.

The CVE-2026-49881 vulnerability is confirmed as a unique pattern
in the Telecom service. The fix (in September 2026 security patch)
should remove the CONTEXT_INCLUDE_CODE flag from this call.
